  "title": "International Criminal Court Wins E.U.’s Top Human Rights Prize",
  "summary": "The International Criminal Court (ICC) receives the European Union’s Top Human Rights Prize, highlighting its role in upholding international law. The prize reflects the Trump administration's efforts to undermine the ICC's work, as seen in its recent sanctions and criticism.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The ICC won the E.U.'s Top Human Rights Prize in recognition of its work in promoting international justice.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The prize is seen as a response to the Trump administration's attempts to weaken the ICC's jurisdiction and authority.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The E.U. supports the ICC's mission, emphasizing its role in upholding human rights.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
